# AGENT BEHAVIOR — NON-NEGOTIABLE

## Context7 — auto-trigger
Always use Context7 MCP before writing code that touches:
- py-clob-client (any method call)
- web3.py (contract interactions)
- aiohttp, websockets (connection patterns)
Never rely on training data for these libraries — fetch docs first, then code.

## Memory MCP — protocole obligatoire

DÉBUT de chaque session :
- Appelle memory search "lp bot polymarket" pour récupérer le contexte
- Lis ce qui remonte avant de toucher au code

FIN de chaque session où du code a changé :
- Sauvegarde dans memory : ce qui a été modifié, pourquoi, et le prochain chantier
- Format : "[date] [fichier:ligne] [changement] → [raison]"

Ce qu'on stocke dans memory :
- Bugs fixés et leur root cause
- Paramètres tuned et les valeurs testées
- Décisions d'architecture et pourquoi
- Prochaine tâche prioritaire

Ce qu'on NE stocke PAS :
- Code complet (trop long, inutile)
- Choses déjà dans les .mdc rules (doublon)

## TASK.md — protocole
- Début de session : lis @.cursor/TASK.md
- Exécute les tâches P0 non cochées dans l'ordre
- Coche [x] avant de commencer, remet [ ] si échec avec raison
- Déplace en "Complété" avec la date quand c'est propre et testé
- Ne passe jamais à P1 sans que tous les P0 soient faits

## Mindset
- Do NOT affirm my statements automatically. Question assumptions. Prioritize truth over agreement.
- If you are unsure whether a file, function, or variable exists: SEARCH FIRST. Never assume.
- Start every reply with the rules you are applying: "Applying: [rule names]"

## Execution protocol (always in this order)
1. SEARCH — use codebase_search or grep to find existing implementations before writing anything
2. READ — open and read the relevant files. Never infer content from filenames alone.
3. PLAN — state what you will change and why, before touching code
4. ACT — make changes file by file. Stop after each file for review.
5. VERIFY — after changes, confirm no imports are broken, no existing tests are affected

## Hard limits — hallucination prevention
- NEVER invent a function, class, or module that you have not seen in the code
- NEVER assume a file exists because CLAUDE.md or AGENTS.md mentions it — verify with ls/grep first
- NEVER generate code that references `dashboard/`, `core/positions_aggregator.py`, or `scripts/positions_cli.py` — these DO NOT EXIST in the repo (doc is stale)
- NEVER suggest `DRY_RUN=false` changes without explicit user confirmation — bot is live on mainnet
- If a config key is not in `config/settings.py`, it does not exist. Do not invent env vars.

## Code quality rules
- All async functions must handle exceptions — no bare `await` without try/except in prod paths
- All changes to `main.py` must preserve the `cancel_all_orders` startup sequence (line ~815)
- Never remove the SIGTERM graceful shutdown handler
- Logging: use `logger.info/warning/error` (loguru) — never `print()`
- Type hints required on all new functions

## Response format
- File references: always `filename.py:line_number`
- When proposing a fix: show diff-style (old → new), not just the new version
- One file at a time. Never batch 5 files in one shot without asking.
